1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Would you drive 446 km of desert with no town, no water? I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,800
This is China's Tarim Desert Highway.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,000
It crosses the Taklamakan, the world's second-largest sand desert.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,200
Nearly the size of Germany, and almost empty.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,400
No village, no farm, no stream the whole way.

6
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:19,200
Double-tap if you'd make this drive.

7
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,400
Keepers in well-houses every 4 km hold back the sand.

8
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:26,000
★ Expert Tip: Fuel up at Luntai and carry water — stops are hours apart.

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,200
Would you drive it, or fly over it?
